Study the script:
```js
var today = new Date();
var hourNow = today.getHours();
var greeting;

if (hourNow > 18) {
  greeting = 'Good evening';
} else if (hourNow > 12) {
  greeting = 'Good afternoon';
} else if (hourNow > 0) {
  greeting = 'Good morning';
} else {
  greeting = 'Welcome';
}

document.write(greeting);
```
What is written on the page when `hourNow` is exactly `12`?

